# Cloudflare Pages headers
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# dicom_toolkit compiles its Rust backend to WASM using threading
# (SharedArrayBuffer). Browsers only enable SharedArrayBuffer when the
# document is cross-origin isolated, which requires BOTH of these headers
# to be served as real HTTP response headers. <meta http-equiv> tags in
# index.html are NOT honored for worker-spawned contexts, so this file is
# the primary mechanism — the meta tags are only a belt-and-suspenders
# fallback for top-level documents.
#
# Picked up automatically by `wrangler pages deploy` from the build output.
# For local dev, use `flutter run -d chrome` with the --web-header flags
# (see .vscode/launch.json "apexo-flutter (web, COOP/COEP)").
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
